1
00:00:06,938 --> 00:00:09,389
On 9 April 1954,

2
00:00:09,429 --> 00:00:13,569
French aircraft dropped 195 tons of
supplies into the Điện Biên Phủ valley.

3
00:00:14,969 --> 00:00:16,889
The French recovered only 6 tons.

4
00:00:16,929 --> 00:00:18,089
Six tons.

5
00:00:19,429 --> 00:00:21,571
The rest never reached its recipients.

6
00:00:21,611 --> 00:00:25,655
Nearly 5 months earlier, the air route was
one reason the French chose this site.

7
00:00:25,695 --> 00:00:30,242
The widest valley in the Northwest,
room for an air-land base fed by air.

8
00:00:30,282 --> 00:00:32,255
The French command believed two things.

9
00:00:32,295 --> 00:00:34,135
The Vietnamese can't bring big guns.

10
00:00:34,962 --> 00:00:37,175
And can't feed a large force for long,

11
00:00:37,215 --> 00:00:39,446
on roads hundreds of kilometers long.

12
00:00:39,486 --> 00:00:42,206
The complex's artillery
chief, Lt. Col. Piroth,

13
00:00:42,246 --> 00:00:46,086
promised no opposing gun would fire
over 3 rounds without being destroyed,

14
00:00:46,126 --> 00:00:47,648
per the Vietnam News Agency.

15
00:00:47,688 --> 00:00:48,828
Three rounds.

16
00:00:51,608 --> 00:00:55,768
Yet from late March, no plane could
land on the Mường Thanh airstrip.

17
00:00:55,808 --> 00:00:58,622
It lay in range of Vietnamese
artillery and AA guns.

18
00:00:58,662 --> 00:01:01,484
On 7 May, the fortified
complex was no more.

19
00:01:01,524 --> 00:01:05,504
Why did the French command choose
Điện Biên Phủ, then lose right there?

20
00:01:08,182 --> 00:01:10,805
This battle is often told
as a foregone conclusion.

21
00:01:10,845 --> 00:01:15,025
But that outcome was made
choice by choice, by both sides.

22
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:18,257
Those two beliefs, and
why the valley was chosen,

23
00:01:18,297 --> 00:01:22,277
turned back, one by one, on those who
made them, through three decisions.

24
00:01:23,937 --> 00:01:28,496
First, the French command turned the
valley into a "hedgehog" fed by airlift.

25
00:01:28,536 --> 00:01:31,736
Second, on 26 January, the
Vietnamese turned to "strike surely,"

26
00:01:31,776 --> 00:01:34,359
"advance surely": guns
out, positions rebuilt.

27
00:01:34,399 --> 00:01:40,015
Third, from phase 2, trenches closed in,
split the airstrip, sealed the French sky.

28
00:01:40,055 --> 00:01:44,615
Each step is checked against two ledgers:
what the French believed or recorded,

29
00:01:44,655 --> 00:01:46,975
and what the Vietnamese
army and people did.

30
00:01:48,643 --> 00:01:52,083
The 3-round promise was tested
on the afternoon of 13 March.

31
00:01:52,123 --> 00:01:54,483
Chosen to lure the Vietnamese main force,

32
00:01:54,523 --> 00:01:58,263
the valley became a trap the
French command set for itself.

33
00:02:04,043 --> 00:02:06,256
In May 1953,

34
00:02:06,296 --> 00:02:09,803
when General Navarre came to Indochina
as French commander-in-chief,

35
00:02:09,843 --> 00:02:12,203
Điện Biên Phủ was not yet in his plan.

36
00:02:13,563 --> 00:02:17,403
The French National Defense Council
approved that plan on 24 July.

37
00:02:18,623 --> 00:02:19,930
The People's Army paper:

38
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:22,023
it aimed to help, within about 18 months,

39
00:02:22,063 --> 00:02:24,943
colonial France
"end the war with honor."

40
00:02:26,623 --> 00:02:28,183
Per Col. Gen. Hoàng Minh Thảo,

41
00:02:28,223 --> 00:02:31,423
Navarre's mobile forces
numbered up to 84 battalions.

42
00:02:31,463 --> 00:02:36,063
But within months, all calculations
converged on one valley in the Northwest.

43
00:02:37,173 --> 00:02:41,414
The cause: the Vietnamese advance into the
Northwest made the French change course.

44
00:02:41,454 --> 00:02:44,373
On 20 November, Operation Castor began.

45
00:02:44,413 --> 00:02:49,254
Six parachute battalions, about 4,500 men,
jumped into Mường Thanh in turn.

46
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:53,554
Three battalions dropped on the first day,
the other three in the days that followed.

47
00:02:54,570 --> 00:02:57,543
The French command saw three
things in its favor here.

48
00:02:57,583 --> 00:02:59,863
The valley is about 18 km long,

49
00:02:59,903 --> 00:03:03,623
and 6 to 8 km wide, the
largest plain in the Northwest.

50
00:03:03,663 --> 00:03:06,183
From here it could shield Upper Laos.

51
00:03:06,223 --> 00:03:10,503
And the ground was broad enough for
an air-land base supplied by air.

52
00:03:10,863 --> 00:03:15,784
Per Nhân Dân newspaper, General Cogny
called Điện Biên Phủ a "fixation abscess."

53
00:03:15,824 --> 00:03:18,204
That phrase reveals their intent.

54
00:03:20,144 --> 00:03:25,284
The French command wanted the valley to
trap and destroy most of the main force.

55
00:03:25,576 --> 00:03:30,416
On 3 December, Navarre issued a directive
accepting battle at Điện Biên Phủ.

56
00:03:31,956 --> 00:03:36,156
On 6 December, the Politburo decided
to launch the Điện Biên Phủ Campaign.

57
00:03:36,196 --> 00:03:40,696
From then on, the valley became a
battlefield both sides had chosen.

58
00:03:40,995 --> 00:03:44,466
In those months, Vietnamese
units set out in secret.

59
00:03:44,506 --> 00:03:47,986
Mr. Trần Quốc Hanh, then a
political officer of Battalion 418,

60
00:03:48,026 --> 00:03:51,126
Division 304, told the
People's Army paper.

61
00:03:51,166 --> 00:03:53,726
"For over a month in
Phú Thọ's bamboo forest,

62
00:03:53,766 --> 00:03:57,606
the troops could not meet the people
or train, for fear of exposure."

63
00:03:59,646 --> 00:04:04,426
The unit's cook also had to pose as a
civilian, buying at many markets.

64
00:04:04,686 --> 00:04:06,406
The trap's site had been chosen.

65
00:04:06,446 --> 00:04:09,206
What remained for the
French was to build it.

66
00:04:11,755 --> 00:04:15,766
In the next weeks, strongpoints rose one
by one in the Mường Thanh valley.

67
00:04:15,806 --> 00:04:19,566
The first decision was the French
command's: make this place a hedgehog.

68
00:04:19,606 --> 00:04:21,206
What was the hedgehog made of?

69
00:04:21,246 --> 00:04:26,646
49 strongpoints in three sectors: North,
Central, and South at Hồng Cúm (Isabelle).

70
00:04:26,686 --> 00:04:30,739
The commander was Colonel Christian de
Castries, later made Brigadier General.

71
00:04:30,779 --> 00:04:34,886
At the campaign's opening, about
11,800 French troops were there.

72
00:04:36,106 --> 00:04:38,786
Firepower: two battalions
of 105 mm howitzers,

73
00:04:38,826 --> 00:04:41,686
plus 155 mm guns and tanks.

74
00:04:42,966 --> 00:04:46,344
Artillery was under Lt. Col.
Piroth, who made the 3-round promise.

75
00:04:46,384 --> 00:04:51,764
Per VNA, he thought the Vietnamese could
bring only small guns and mortars in.

76
00:04:53,247 --> 00:04:56,400
Bringing in heavy artillery,
to him, was impossible.

77
00:04:56,440 --> 00:05:01,868
The model had a name: the "hedgehog,"
an air-land base to block the main force.

78
00:05:01,908 --> 00:05:04,025
But this hedgehog could not feed itself.

79
00:05:04,065 --> 00:05:07,782
The valley was hundreds of km from
Hanoi, so everything had to fly in.

80
00:05:07,822 --> 00:05:10,886
From November, an airlift
linked the delta to the valley.

81
00:05:10,926 --> 00:05:14,799
Each day, dozens of transport flights
brought in about 200 tons of cargo.

82
00:05:14,839 --> 00:05:17,614
The valley had two airstrips,
Mường Thanh and Hồng Cúm.

83
00:05:17,654 --> 00:05:21,566
Ammunition, food, reinforcements:
all arrived by air.

84
00:05:21,606 --> 00:05:24,086
On 24 December, per Nhân Dân,

85
00:05:24,126 --> 00:05:26,766
General Navarre told troops
at Điện Biên Phủ that

86
00:05:26,806 --> 00:05:29,546
the battle could only turn
out well for the French.

87
00:05:30,919 --> 00:05:34,719
But a week later, on 1 January 1954,

88
00:05:34,759 --> 00:05:37,199
he privately wrote about
the chances of success.

89
00:05:37,239 --> 00:05:40,199
According to Nhân Dân,
Navarre wrote: "Two weeks ago,

90
00:05:40,239 --> 00:05:43,119
I put that chance at 100 percent."

91
00:05:44,799 --> 00:05:47,919
Then he admitted that, with
the opposing side reinforcing,

92
00:05:47,959 --> 00:05:49,959
he no longer dared claim as much.

93
00:05:50,724 --> 00:05:52,418
Words to soldiers are one thing.

94
00:05:52,458 --> 00:05:54,478
A private letter is another.

95
00:05:57,215 --> 00:05:59,641
The whole hedgehog stood
on those two beliefs.

96
00:05:59,681 --> 00:06:02,272
If they held, each spine was a wall.

97
00:06:02,312 --> 00:06:06,084
If they were wrong, each spine
only pinned down the man behind it.

98
00:06:06,124 --> 00:06:09,364
The answer was being hauled
over mountains on the other side.

99
00:06:10,734 --> 00:06:13,134
From 16 January, at the
Nà Nhạn forest edge,

100
00:06:13,174 --> 00:06:15,646
Vietnamese guns began
moving to their positions.

101
00:06:15,686 --> 00:06:19,299
With no vehicles, how many people
to move one gun over the mountains?

102
00:06:19,339 --> 00:06:22,339
Mr. Phạm Đức Cư, a
soldier of Battalion 394,

103
00:06:22,379 --> 00:06:25,997
Anti-Aircraft Regiment 367,
told the People's Army paper.

104
00:06:26,037 --> 00:06:30,357
Each 2.4-ton gun took
80 to 100 people to haul.

105
00:06:31,609 --> 00:06:36,209
The road was 15 km long and about 3 meters
wide, winding over Pu Pha Sông peak.

106
00:06:36,249 --> 00:06:38,449
Camouflaged as fast as it was built.

107
00:06:38,489 --> 00:06:41,924
Meals were eaten on the
spot, then back to work.

108
00:06:41,964 --> 00:06:44,484
Mr. Nguyễn Quang Thuận,
a soldier of Company 815,

109
00:06:44,524 --> 00:06:49,734
recalls his commander's shout (People's
Army paper): "Two... three... heave!"

110
00:06:49,774 --> 00:06:53,815
Each shout moved the gun only a few
dozen centimeters up the steep slope.

111
00:06:53,855 --> 00:06:55,392
Nearly 10 nights of this.

112
00:06:55,432 --> 00:06:59,153
Five main-force divisions of the Vietnam
People's Army joined this battle.

113
00:06:59,193 --> 00:07:01,880
Vietnamese guns and mortars:
over 200 of all kinds.

114
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:05,000
Among them: 24 howitzers,
16 heavy mortars,

115
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,767
24 anti-aircraft guns and
dozens of mountain guns.

116
00:07:09,751 --> 00:07:12,071
The 105 mm howitzers were precisely the

117
00:07:12,111 --> 00:07:15,151
heavy guns the French thought
the Vietnamese couldn't bring.

118
00:07:15,191 --> 00:07:19,871
By 25 January, most of those guns were
in position, awaiting the order to fire.

119
00:07:19,911 --> 00:07:22,191
But the moment to fire never came.

120
00:07:23,486 --> 00:07:26,286
Before leaving for the front,
General Võ Nguyên Giáp,

121
00:07:26,326 --> 00:07:31,246
the commander and Front Party secretary,
was advised by President Ho Chi Minh.

122
00:07:35,006 --> 00:07:36,406
On 26 January,

123
00:07:36,446 --> 00:07:40,246
the General, the Party Committee, and
the campaign command changed course.

124
00:07:40,286 --> 00:07:44,466
From "strike fast, win fast" to
"strike surely, advance surely."

125
00:07:46,114 --> 00:07:47,754
The reason was clearly recorded.

126
00:07:47,794 --> 00:07:51,914
Troops and fortifications in the valley
had grown far denser since planning.

127
00:07:51,954 --> 00:07:53,874
Vietnamese guns weren't all in place.

128
00:07:53,914 --> 00:07:56,953
And a fast attack no
longer guaranteed victory.

129
00:07:56,993 --> 00:08:01,266
That very night, 26 January, guns
just hauled in were ordered back out.

130
00:08:01,306 --> 00:08:04,186
Mr. Nguyễn Quang Thuận recalled in
the People's Army paper

131
00:08:04,226 --> 00:08:07,006
that the order came "like a thunderclap."

132
00:08:08,239 --> 00:08:10,653
Once explained, the units obeyed strictly.

133
00:08:10,693 --> 00:08:12,043
Hauling in was hard enough.

134
00:08:12,083 --> 00:08:16,055
Hauling out, then rebuilding positions,
meant starting all over again.

135
00:08:16,095 --> 00:08:19,055
On 1 February, at Dốc Chuối,
on a narrow road,

136
00:08:19,095 --> 00:08:23,555
Mountain on one side, chasm on the other.
The winch cable suddenly snapped.

137
00:08:24,315 --> 00:08:27,355
An anti-aircraft gun weighing
over 2 tons slid downhill.

138
00:08:28,195 --> 00:08:31,175
Gun commander Tô Vĩnh Diện
lunged to chock the wheels.

139
00:08:31,995 --> 00:08:35,060
The gun didn't go over the edge.
He heroically gave his life.

140
00:08:37,607 --> 00:08:42,747
By the morning of 5 February, the third
day of Tết Giáp Ngọ, hauling out was done.

141
00:08:43,394 --> 00:08:45,594
The new positions differed sharply.

142
00:08:45,634 --> 00:08:48,154
Each gun sat in a bunker
on the mountainside.

143
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:52,394
Some mountain guns fired directly;
the 105 mm howitzers stayed far back.

144
00:08:52,434 --> 00:08:55,354
Besides real positions, the
Vietnamese built dummy ones.

145
00:08:55,394 --> 00:09:00,955
Per VNA, French artillery never detected
the Vietnamese gun positions in that time.

146
00:09:00,995 --> 00:09:03,035
Was that decision right or wrong?

147
00:09:05,254 --> 00:09:07,678
The answer came on the
afternoon of 13 March.

148
00:09:07,718 --> 00:09:09,729
At 5:05 p.m. on 13 March,

149
00:09:09,769 --> 00:09:12,569
dozens of Vietnamese guns
shelled Him Lam (Béatrice).

150
00:09:15,869 --> 00:09:17,629
The Điện Biên Phủ Campaign began.

151
00:09:17,669 --> 00:09:20,369
The 3-round promise now faced a real test.

152
00:09:21,729 --> 00:09:23,197
French artillery fired back.

153
00:09:23,237 --> 00:09:26,369
As the real guns fired,
dummy positions flashed too.

154
00:09:26,409 --> 00:09:30,489
According to VNA, most French
shells fell on the decoy positions.

155
00:09:30,529 --> 00:09:33,209
Others hit sturdy covered fortifications.

156
00:09:33,249 --> 00:09:36,489
That night, deputy squad leader
Phan Đình Giót of Company 58,

157
00:09:36,529 --> 00:09:39,809
threw himself over the embrasure
to open the way for his comrades.

158
00:09:41,069 --> 00:09:45,429
Him Lam was taken that night; Độc Lập
(Gabrielle) on the morning of 15 March.

159
00:09:45,469 --> 00:09:47,829
17 March: Bản Kéo
(Anne-Marie) surrendered.

160
00:09:47,869 --> 00:09:49,881
The valley's north entrance was open.

161
00:09:49,921 --> 00:09:51,761
Per the People's Army paper,

162
00:09:51,801 --> 00:09:55,461
before the battle, Lt. Col. Piroth said:
"I have more guns than I need."

163
00:09:56,917 --> 00:10:01,412
According to VNA, around Him Lam
hill, Piroth had about 6,000 shells fired.

164
00:10:01,452 --> 00:10:03,380
Yet Vietnamese guns weren't silenced.

165
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:05,760
The 3-round promise could not be kept.

166
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:10,412
By the French command's calculations,
those guns could not be here.

167
00:10:10,452 --> 00:10:12,412
The first belief was wrong.

168
00:10:14,149 --> 00:10:16,229
Even later, despite more recon flights,

169
00:10:16,269 --> 00:10:18,762
French guns never found
Vietnamese gun positions.

170
00:10:18,802 --> 00:10:22,202
Anti-Aircraft Regiment 367 also
fought from the first days;

171
00:10:22,242 --> 00:10:24,701
by the end of phase 1 it
had downed 14 aircraft.

172
00:10:24,741 --> 00:10:26,581
Per Nhân Dân, after the first clash,

173
00:10:26,621 --> 00:10:29,801
the French expeditionary corps
added about 4,000 more troops.

174
00:10:31,001 --> 00:10:32,161
On 27 March,

175
00:10:32,201 --> 00:10:35,012
a French plane landed at Mường Thanh
for the last time.

176
00:10:35,052 --> 00:10:37,945
From late March, under
Vietnamese artillery and flak,

177
00:10:37,985 --> 00:10:40,012
the airstrip could take no more planes.

178
00:10:40,052 --> 00:10:42,092
Supply now relied on airdrops alone.

179
00:10:42,132 --> 00:10:45,832
On 30 March, phase 2 began
and ran to the end of April.

180
00:10:48,652 --> 00:10:53,332
The Vietnamese hit the eastern heights and
dug trenches to split and hold the runway.

181
00:10:53,372 --> 00:10:58,132
Decision three went further: from phase 2,
trenches split the runway, meter by meter.

182
00:10:58,172 --> 00:11:03,252
Eastern heights C1 (Éliane 1), E, D and
A1 (Éliane 2) shielded the Central sector.

183
00:11:03,292 --> 00:11:06,680
Vietnamese forces assaulted each
height, tightening the ring.

184
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:10,680
Some heights were fought for all of
phase 2, and fully taken only in phase 3.

185
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:15,092
Early April: another parachute battalion
jumped plane by plane, taking 3 nights.

186
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:17,026
Phase 2 was the trench phase.

187
00:11:17,066 --> 00:11:18,612
Trenches were 1.7 meters deep.

188
00:11:18,652 --> 00:11:21,972
Per the People's Army paper, trenches
ran "hundreds of kilometers."

189
00:11:22,012 --> 00:11:26,389
Trenches reached each strongpoint, cut the
airstrip, and brought charges to bunkers.

190
00:11:26,429 --> 00:11:30,766
Also in early April, days of rain flooded
the trenches and collapsed their walls.

191
00:11:30,806 --> 00:11:33,146
But the people in them kept digging.

192
00:11:35,645 --> 00:11:39,192
Each new stretch of trench was
ground the hedgehog had to give up.

193
00:11:39,232 --> 00:11:41,032
Spines can be pulled one by one.

194
00:11:41,072 --> 00:11:45,726
But the hedgehog still had one lifeline
feeding it: parachutes from the sky.

195
00:11:45,766 --> 00:11:48,137
On that 9 April, in the
sky over the valley,

196
00:11:48,177 --> 00:11:52,557
195 tons of cargo were dropped, and
only 6 tons reached the recipients.

197
00:11:54,257 --> 00:11:57,636
The fortified complex needed about
200 tons of ammunition a day.

198
00:11:57,676 --> 00:12:02,276
But per VNA, at best the French
collected only about 100 tons.

199
00:12:04,163 --> 00:12:06,963
To avoid flak, planes
had to drop from high up,

200
00:12:07,003 --> 00:12:09,587
and some cargo fell into
Vietnamese positions.

201
00:12:09,627 --> 00:12:13,027
Mr. Trần Xuân Kình, a soldier
of Anti-Aircraft Regiment 367,

202
00:12:13,067 --> 00:12:16,920
told Nhân Dân that the anti-aircraft
gunners' job was to hit planes,

203
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:19,907
to "keep the sky quiet" for ground forces.

204
00:12:21,422 --> 00:12:24,982
He recalled a time his company
fired without downing a plane,

205
00:12:25,022 --> 00:12:28,741
but the planes scattered and dropped
chutes outside French positions.

206
00:12:28,781 --> 00:12:30,966
On the ground, the
trenches kept advancing.

207
00:12:31,006 --> 00:12:35,672
From 16 April, trenches from two sides
met, splitting the Mường Thanh airstrip.

208
00:12:35,712 --> 00:12:40,312
From the night of 20 April, at Hill A1,
a silent dig began underground.

209
00:12:40,352 --> 00:12:43,112
Engineer Company 83, Regiment 151,

210
00:12:43,152 --> 00:12:44,861
dug a tunnel into the hill.

211
00:12:44,901 --> 00:12:48,361
How could they dig to a strongpoint's
foot without being detected?

212
00:12:50,416 --> 00:12:53,256
Colonel Nguyễn Bội Giong,
then a High Command envoy,

213
00:12:53,296 --> 00:12:57,066
told the People's Army paper that the
digging had to solve three things.

214
00:12:57,106 --> 00:12:58,571
Stay undetected.

215
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:01,255
Hide the mouth when
dumping soil, hold course.

216
00:13:01,295 --> 00:13:03,075
And the diggers must not suffocate.

217
00:13:04,299 --> 00:13:06,499
Direction was held by a small compass,

218
00:13:06,539 --> 00:13:09,940
under a nearly covered flashlight,
glowing "like a firefly."

219
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:13,125
Air was changed with
bamboo fans, in shifts.

220
00:13:13,165 --> 00:13:17,045
On 28 April, the Mường Thanh
airstrip was completely neutralized.

221
00:13:17,085 --> 00:13:22,199
By late April, phase 2 closed; A1 and C1
still weren't fully in Vietnamese hands.

222
00:13:22,239 --> 00:13:27,019
On 1 May, phase 3 began, to finish off
the last heights in the East.

223
00:13:28,298 --> 00:13:31,658
According to Nhân Dân and
VNA, by the final stage,

224
00:13:31,698 --> 00:13:34,411
about a third of the drops
hit Vietnamese positions.

225
00:13:34,451 --> 00:13:36,811
H6 rocket launchers joined in this phase.

226
00:13:38,163 --> 00:13:41,883
Under Hill A1, the tunnel was finished
after about 15 days and nights.

227
00:13:44,844 --> 00:13:47,084
At 8:30 p.m. on 6 May,

228
00:13:47,124 --> 00:13:50,164
nearly a ton of charges at the
tunnel's end was detonated.

229
00:13:52,455 --> 00:13:56,336
The man who set it off was squad leader
Nguyễn Văn Bạch, Engineer Company 83.

230
00:13:56,376 --> 00:13:59,636
That blast was the signal to
attack along the whole front.

231
00:14:01,231 --> 00:14:04,622
At dawn on 7 May, the Vietnamese
took full control of Hill A1.

232
00:14:04,662 --> 00:14:07,622
That same day, the Vietnamese
began the general assault.

233
00:14:07,662 --> 00:14:09,496
Three decisions, one full circle.

234
00:14:09,536 --> 00:14:10,714
Heavy guns had arrived.

235
00:14:10,754 --> 00:14:12,560
The French had lost the sky.

236
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:16,520
The second belief remained: the
Vietnamese could not sustain a large force

237
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,380
for long, far from their rear.

238
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:24,040
That belief was tested on the supply
routes, behind the mountain range.

239
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:27,280
After 56 days and nights, by 7 May,

240
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:29,273
the field left two kinds of figures.

241
00:14:29,313 --> 00:14:31,933
The first is the official
figure of the battle.

242
00:14:32,661 --> 00:14:35,514
16,200 enemy troops killed or captured.

243
00:14:35,554 --> 00:14:38,074
62 aircraft shot down or destroyed.

244
00:14:38,994 --> 00:14:41,354
The second is the figure of human effort.

245
00:14:42,151 --> 00:14:43,151
Per Nhân Dân,

246
00:14:43,191 --> 00:14:45,311
the French command thought the Vietnamese

247
00:14:45,351 --> 00:14:47,791
could not mass over 2
divisions that far away.

248
00:14:47,831 --> 00:14:49,551
Yet 5 divisions were brought up.

249
00:14:49,591 --> 00:14:52,191
The main-force troops alone
numbered about 40,000.

250
00:14:53,411 --> 00:14:55,998
Feeding those 5 divisions
fell to the whole rear.

251
00:14:56,038 --> 00:14:58,010
How much can one bicycle carry?

252
00:14:58,050 --> 00:15:01,848
At first, each cargo bicycle
carried only 80 to 100 kilograms.

253
00:15:01,888 --> 00:15:05,208
Then porters tied a roughly 1 m
bamboo pole to the handlebars,

254
00:15:05,248 --> 00:15:06,512
to steer: the "tay ngai."

255
00:15:06,552 --> 00:15:10,552
After the improvement, each bicycle
carried 200 to 300 kilograms.

256
00:15:11,853 --> 00:15:16,135
Porter Ma Văn Thắng of Phú Thọ once
carried over 300 kg on his bicycle.

257
00:15:16,175 --> 00:15:19,215
The campaign had over
260,000 frontline porters,

258
00:15:19,255 --> 00:15:22,975
nearly 21,000 cargo bicycles,
and over 23,000 tons of rice.

259
00:15:23,619 --> 00:15:26,839
Those figures appear in none
of the French calculations.

260
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:31,047
The French colonial hedgehog
lived on air routes.

261
00:15:31,087 --> 00:15:34,410
The other side lived on human
shoulders and cargo bicycles.

262
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:37,010
The cost was recorded too: per VTV,

263
00:15:37,130 --> 00:15:40,370
4,020 Vietnamese officers and
soldiers gave their lives,

264
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:44,790
792 went missing, and 9,118 were wounded.

265
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:49,800
Those two beliefs collapsed,

266
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:54,440
because the Vietnamese army and people did
both things the French command ruled out.

267
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,707
At 5:30 p.m. on 7 May,

268
00:15:58,747 --> 00:16:00,867
Led by company commander Tạ Quốc Luật,

269
00:16:00,907 --> 00:16:04,913
Division 312, the assault team advanced
on the complex's command bunker.

270
00:16:04,953 --> 00:16:10,041
In Nhân Dân he recalled: as he drew
near, he shouted in French: "Hands up!"

271
00:16:10,081 --> 00:16:13,869
General de Castries was captured
along with his entire staff.

272
00:16:13,909 --> 00:16:16,669
By his account, de Castries took the phone

273
00:16:16,709 --> 00:16:19,001
and ordered French troops
there to surrender.

274
00:16:19,041 --> 00:16:23,201
Atop the command bunker now flew the flag
"Determined to Fight, Determined to Win."

275
00:16:23,916 --> 00:16:27,756
The next day, 8 May, President Ho
Chi Minh wrote to praise the troops,

276
00:16:27,796 --> 00:16:31,936
porters, Youth Volunteers and the people
of the Northwest, with one instruction.

277
00:16:38,651 --> 00:16:42,691
First, the French command's decision:
build a hedgehog on two beliefs,

278
00:16:42,731 --> 00:16:44,680
then force it to live off the sky.

279
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:47,960
Second, Vietnam's army and people
hauled guns over mountains,

280
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,537
then out again: "strike
surely, advance surely."

281
00:16:50,577 --> 00:16:53,097
Third, the Vietnamese
tightened the trenches,

282
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:56,296
split the airstrip, and took the last
of the complex's sky.

283
00:16:56,336 --> 00:16:58,576
A feat of the Vietnam People's Army,

284
00:16:58,616 --> 00:17:01,336
led by the Party and
President Ho Chi Minh.

285
00:17:01,376 --> 00:17:03,536
Lt. Col. Piroth promised no opposing gun

286
00:17:03,576 --> 00:17:06,596
would fire over 3 rounds
without being destroyed.

287
00:17:07,841 --> 00:17:13,181
Those guns were hauled over the mountains
by human hands, once in and once out.

288
00:17:13,281 --> 00:17:16,546
Each shout on the slope moved
the gun a few dozen centimeters.

289
00:17:16,586 --> 00:17:20,259
Today, General de Castries's command
bunker remains structurally intact.

290
00:17:20,299 --> 00:17:23,538
On Hill A1, the demolition crater
is still there, intact.

291
00:17:23,578 --> 00:17:27,938
Nearby, the A1 National Martyrs'
Cemetery holds 645 graves.

292
00:17:27,978 --> 00:17:32,938
Per an August 2026 report in
Văn hóa newspaper and VNA,

293
00:17:33,658 --> 00:17:37,778
10 graves have full information,
39 have partial information.

294
00:17:39,738 --> 00:17:42,618
596 graves have no information yet.

